  "scope": "All twenty-four actual arithmetic-model, center-lattice, exponent, period, primitive-point and point-equality proofs at the complete stated source scopes; full N1c remains separate.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Fixed Hermitian space and complete local scope",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Read all PUN1-PUN24 proofs. The ternary quadratic norm argument retains square delta, all finite places including dyadic places, and every real embedding. The Hermitian local-global induction handles the isotropic zero case and local cancellation, including split algebras. The actual Host unramified condition permits the common trace-dual fractional ideal to be scaled to unimodular lattices. This preserves the given Gm and xi, rather than merely producing an isomorphic replacement space. The zero-xi case is handled by perfection forcing rank zero."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Full arithmetic lattice model",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Compared the actual LatModel and ModelsOf contracts. Half-level congruence and dual perfection give equality with the full principal congruence kernel for lcm(M,A). The coset bound, bounded-powers flag stabilizer and odd-prime congruence argument supply the original index and free-action fields. One transvection modulus is chosen before all vectors and scalars. ModelsOf, ModelBase and NegXi remain conditional on the supplied FamilyUnif."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual center lattice and exact exponent",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The center is an injective additive skew-matrix group of the original dimension. Finite index, without normality, gives finite generation and the full rational span of the actual zGam. The adapted projective cusp lattice gives the precise different and ideal factors. The source prE divides kappa0 by two: the resulting one-half rational trace is checked by the trace-one host element, not by an invalid integral division by two. General basis transport uses the correct transpose and conjugate matrices. The complete ExpoMatch endpoint retains A=1."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual primitive line and nonreduced test rings",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The semicharacter alpha(Pa)=exp(pi*i*B(a,w0*a)) and Appell-Humbert factors specify the original line, its rigidification, symmetry, adjoint and cubical structures. Positivity yields algebraization and perfect B yields a principal polarization. The dual Picard universal property for every scheme, including nonreduced schemes, gives the full KTriv for every C-algebra. This is stronger than checking only complex-valued points. The original IsAHframe transformation direction and tangent dual-number condition were compared directly."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Weil sign, original markings and every scalar extension",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The multiplication order in the literal commutator gives exp(-2*pi*i*B(a,b)/n), the required negative Weil sign. Every positive torsion level, the same f_n and nu_n, both half/full markings and the exact TateIso are retained. Obj.geom is verified after every C-to-k scalar extension, including noncontinuous embeddings, by algebraic finite-etale torsion base change. The given moduli representation supplies the actual point."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Point equality and marked genus nonemptiness",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The actual semicharacter shows that an integral marked isometry preserves the primitive line, not only its polarization. This gives the complete point_eq_iff_isometry_closed contract. Local unit-norm surjectivity constructs a profinite lift with the correct norm and residue simultaneously, hence all compatible f_n and the original root identity at every prescribed sigma. No global norm solution is assumed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Remaining uniformization scope",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The full FamilyUnif definition was compared, including finite components, holomorphic families, theta frames and local lifting. Individual points, their equality and ModelsOf on a supplied family do not imply N1c. That original global holomorphic and normalized-family producer, and the later spanning inputs, remain open. No selected whole leaf is closed by this component."
    }
  ],
